cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived software release."
type: software
title: sequoia-boost
abstract: >-
  sequoia-boost is a pure Rust implementation of gradient boosted decision
  trees modeled on XGBoost's public algorithms and interfaces. It supports
  exact, histogram, and approximate tree construction, regression,
  classification, count models, ranking objectives, categorical features,
  missing values, monotone constraints, interaction constraints, DART, and
  linear boosters. Models provide early stopping, cross validation, feature
  importance, leaf prediction, TreeSHAP values, native serialization, and
  numeric-tree XGBoost JSON interoperability. Dense, sparse, CSV, and libsvm
  data are supported. The crate targets Rust applications that need CPU-based
  gradient boosting without C or C++ linkage. It requires Rust 1.86 or newer
  and uses Rayon for parallel histogram construction.
